@startuml
' House preamble for cloud / infrastructure diagrams with the official AWS Architecture Icons
' (PlantUML stdlib awslib20 = awslabs/aws-icons-for-plantuml v20.0). Start a diagram as this
' file followed by templates/skeleton-aws.puml; edit only below the end marker.
' Rule: when the sources name an AWS service, draw it with its icon macro, never a plain shape.
' Each service needs its own include, below the marker. Paths proven on PlantUML 1.2026.8:
'   !include <awslib20/Analytics/Redshift>                              Redshift(alias, "label", "tech")
'   !include <awslib20/Storage/SimpleStorageService>                    S3 service
'   !include <awslib20/Storage/SimpleStorageServiceBucket>              one S3 bucket
'   !include <awslib20/Analytics/Glue>
'   !include <awslib20/Analytics/Athena>
'   !include <awslib20/Analytics/LakeFormation>
'   !include <awslib20/Analytics/QuickSight>
'   !include <awslib20/Containers/ElasticKubernetesService>             EKS
'   !include <awslib20/ApplicationIntegration/ManagedWorkflowsforApacheAirflow>   MWAA (Airflow)
'   !include <awslib20/ApplicationIntegration/StepFunctions>
'   !include <awslib20/ApplicationIntegration/EventBridge>
'   !include <awslib20/ApplicationIntegration/SimpleQueueService>       SQS
'   !include <awslib20/ApplicationIntegration/SimpleNotificationService> SNS
'   !include <awslib20/Compute/EC2>  <awslib20/Compute/EC2Instance>  <awslib20/Compute/Lambda>
'   !include <awslib20/Database/RDS>  <awslib20/Database/Aurora>
'   !include <awslib20/ManagementGovernance/CloudWatch>
'   !include <awslib20/SecurityIdentityCompliance/IdentityandAccessManagement>   IAM
'   !include <awslib20/NetworkingContentDelivery/VirtualPrivateCloud>
'   !include <awslib20/NetworkingContentDelivery/ElasticLoadBalancing>
'   !include <awslib20/NetworkingContentDelivery/VPCInternetGateway>
'   !include <awslib20/General/Users>
' Macro form: Service(alias, "label", "technology"). Always pass a real technology
' ("nginx, Elastic IP", "PostgreSQL"): a 2-argument call fails ("Function not found") and
' an empty "" prints "[]" (lint ERROR icon-empty-tech).
' GenericGroup(alias, "Stage") { } frames a stage or any grouping that is not an AWS construct.
' Groups nest like the AWS architecture guideline: AWSCloudGroup > RegionGroup > VPCGroup >
' AvailabilityZoneGroup > PublicSubnetGroup / PrivateSubnetGroup > AutoScalingGroupGroup.
' Sibling groups (two AZs) sit side by side, row for row, with pins between corresponding
' elements (rp1 -[hidden]right- rp2, db1 -[hidden]right- db2) plus explicit -down-> edges
' (reference § Layout moves, E). Orthogonal edges stay on: icon labels are short.
' `hide stereotype` is required: otherwise every icon prints its «EC2Instance» stereotype.
' house-preamble-begin
' Knob LEGEND_FRAME: colour of the thin frame around the legend ("transparent" removes it).
!$LEGEND_FRAME = "#999999"
!theme plain
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam wrapWidth 300
skinparam maxMessageSize 300
skinparam legendBackgroundColor transparent
skinparam legendBorderColor $LEGEND_FRAME
skinparam nodesep 40
skinparam ranksep 50
hide stereotype
<style>
root { FontName "Helvetica"; FontSize 12 }
title { FontSize 16 }
</style>
!include <awslib20/AWSCommon>
!include <awslib20/Groups/AWSCloud>
!include <awslib20/Groups/Generic>
!include <awslib20/Groups/Region>
!include <awslib20/Groups/VPC>
!include <awslib20/Groups/AvailabilityZone>
!include <awslib20/Groups/PublicSubnet>
!include <awslib20/Groups/PrivateSubnet>
!include <awslib20/Groups/AutoScalingGroup>
' Numbered steps (optional, STYLE rule 16): $step(1) prints a blue badge in a label, an edge label
' or a legend table row. Knob STEP_BADGE: the badge colour.
!$STEP_BADGE = "#1565C0"
!function $step($n)
!return "<back:" + $STEP_BADGE + "><color:#FFFFFF><b> " + $n + " </b></color></back>"
!endfunction
' house-preamble-end
